     "result_text_tail": "ers could be hired in time, and the mobile delay costs more than a Copilot slip. A second independent check found all 57 numbers taken from the pack match it and no arithmetic errors. It did catch a timeline contradiction and some wording, which I fixed.\n\n**Numbers:** 174 in total: 57 quoted directly from the briefing pack, 116 calculated from them (each with its formula in the workbook), and one value I chose. There are no \"?\" placeholders. Every number rests on that one pack, so none could be checked against a second source.\n\n**Choices I made since you weren't available:**\n- The deep 30\u201360 slide format, written as a client-style diagnostic, in the navy theme.\n- The 850-request allowance, rounded down from the 854 that keeps margin at 75%.\n- I read the 105% target as retention measured over calendar 2028.\n- I assumed the rewrite frees the 14 engineers from Q3 2027. The pack gives no end date for the rewrite, so the CTO needs to confirm this.\n- Out of scope: building your own AI model, changing the base plan's price, and customers outside 3\u201350-technician contractors.\n\nThe QA check's one remaining warning is that the two-quarter delay is written in words in the pack, so the script can't match the figure; the value is correct.\n\nI can switch theme, cut the deck to a shorter version, or rework it around a different launch scenario.\n\nFiles are in `./deliverable/`:\n- `brightwork-dispatch-copilot.pptx`\n- `brightwork-dispatch-copilot-sources.xlsx`\n- `brightwork-dispatch-copilot.json`"
